WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.458
(cackling)

00:00:06.458 --> 00:00:09.348
(screams)

00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:11.848
(eerie music)

00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:19.241
(yells)

00:00:19.241 --> 00:00:20.655
- Ow, you stepped on my toe.

00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:21.684
- I apologize.

00:00:21.684 --> 00:00:22.982
That was my mistake.

00:00:22.982 --> 00:00:25.565
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:29.365
- It's Halloween, it's
the best time of year,

00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:30.226
everybody knows it.

00:00:30.226 --> 00:00:32.354
- Today we're at Knott's
Scary Farm to become monsters

00:00:32.354 --> 00:00:34.552
and crawl around in fog and scare people.

00:00:34.552 --> 00:00:36.370
- So, we're gonna put on some
effects makeup and costumes,

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.596
and become another person entirely.

00:00:38.596 --> 00:00:40.089
And for The Try Guys it's gonna really

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:41.647
bring out our inner demon.

00:00:41.647 --> 00:00:42.689
(screams)

00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:44.993
- My name is John Cook, I
am an entertainment designer

00:00:44.993 --> 00:00:46.466
here for Knott's Scary Farm.

00:00:46.466 --> 00:00:47.996
We hire about 1,000 people in

00:00:47.996 --> 00:00:49.686
and we transform them into monsters.

00:00:49.686 --> 00:00:50.662
We teach them everything.

00:00:50.662 --> 00:00:52.183
We put them in their costumes, makeup,

00:00:52.183 --> 00:00:54.450
to get everything ready and
then we lead to the charge,

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.195
get them out there and
just terrifying people.

00:00:56.195 --> 00:00:58.411
- How does one become a monster?

00:00:58.411 --> 00:01:00.328
- Not only do you have to
apply for a normal job,

00:01:00.328 --> 00:01:01.827
then you come down and we
put you through the ringer.

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:04.594
We ask you guys to pretend
you're Satan ordering a coffee,

00:01:04.594 --> 00:01:05.454
and we just see how you do.

00:01:05.454 --> 00:01:07.347
- I don't like this at all.

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:09.120
- Apparently, Ned is big old baby.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.386
- I'm super afraid of haunted houses.

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:13.209
- I'm also like, " Hey,
Try Guys, let's go watch

00:01:13.209 --> 00:01:14.366
"A horror movie!".

00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:16.052
Zach goes, "(beep) yeah!"

00:01:16.052 --> 00:01:17.911
Keith goes, "All right, I
got nothing else to do."

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.328
Ned goes, "Oh, is it rated R?

00:01:21.321 --> 00:01:23.076
"Is there gore?"

00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:25.685
- However, I do have a theater background.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.673
I think I'll be great with
coming up with character,

00:01:27.673 --> 00:01:30.842
getting into the physicality
of it, doing weird voices.

00:01:30.842 --> 00:01:34.467
My goal today is to get through
this without getting scared.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.821
- I'm such a friendly guy.

00:01:35.821 --> 00:01:37.706
It's tough for me to make
people sad and upset.

00:01:37.706 --> 00:01:39.596
- I think Keith is gonna have so much fun.

00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:41.230
- My goal is to be the most unique monster

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.307
anybody has ever seen in a theme park,

00:01:43.307 --> 00:01:45.344
and I want them to scream so loud

00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:46.866
that they also fall in love.

00:01:46.866 --> 00:01:48.383
- This is honestly a
dream come true for me.

00:01:48.383 --> 00:01:50.561
I'm so giddy I cannot control it.

00:01:50.561 --> 00:01:53.967
- Zach loves dark (beep), and
I'm rooting for him to really

00:01:53.967 --> 00:01:56.857
step up his game and be
bigger than his actual body.

00:01:56.857 --> 00:01:57.855
- I'm not a scary person.

00:01:57.855 --> 00:02:00.213
I've never intimidate anybody in my life,

00:02:00.213 --> 00:02:02.091
so my goal today, I
want to scare somebody.

00:02:02.091 --> 00:02:03.779
I want to see when I get in all the makeup

00:02:03.779 --> 00:02:06.185
can I inhabit a character,
can I scare some people

00:02:06.185 --> 00:02:07.691
the way that I never get to in real life.

00:02:07.691 --> 00:02:09.493
- I feel like everyone
says you put a costume on

00:02:09.493 --> 00:02:12.047
during October, for me
the other 11 months,

00:02:12.047 --> 00:02:14.163
that's when I'm wearing my
costume, my good costume.

00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:16.453
- Eugene is kind of just like a demon.

00:02:16.453 --> 00:02:17.286
- Literally, a demon.

00:02:17.286 --> 00:02:20.524
- I am most excited about
getting in touch with the inner,

00:02:20.524 --> 00:02:23.732
crazy Halloween demon that
I know has resided within me

00:02:23.732 --> 00:02:25.043
ever since I was a child.

00:02:25.043 --> 00:02:29.609
I really want to terrorize
as many people as possible

00:02:29.609 --> 00:02:32.271
so that they never forget my demon face.

00:02:32.271 --> 00:02:34.383
- So, how do we turn
these four beautiful boys

00:02:34.383 --> 00:02:37.101
into four terrifying monsters?

00:02:37.101 --> 00:02:38.660
- I don't know, do we even need masks?

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:39.493
- [All] Oh!

00:02:39.493 --> 00:02:40.418
- Oh, nice!

00:02:40.418 --> 00:02:41.751
- Okay, John!

00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:44.305
- You're gonna go through
the transformation process.

00:02:44.305 --> 00:02:46.103
We're gonna get you
fitted with some costumes.

00:02:46.103 --> 00:02:47.511
- We're gonna fit you in some shirts

00:02:47.511 --> 00:02:48.965
and some dusters and vests, okay?

00:02:48.965 --> 00:02:49.990
There you go

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.452
- [Keith] You and Ned are like twinsies.

00:02:51.452 --> 00:02:52.510
- [Zach] Yeah!

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.408
- We're eternal twins.

00:02:54.408 --> 00:02:56.692
- I cannot show up to Ghost
Town in the same outfit as Ned.

00:02:56.692 --> 00:02:58.106
- Forever!
(laughing)

00:02:58.106 --> 00:02:59.537
- Looking at us, how would think

00:02:59.537 --> 00:03:02.002
we should be crafted into monsters?

00:03:02.002 --> 00:03:04.731
- Well, Ghost Town Knott's
Scary Farm is where it started.

00:03:04.731 --> 00:03:07.905
We are looking for dead,
decayed ghost town citizens.

00:03:07.905 --> 00:03:10.973
The story is that the
green witch cursed people

00:03:10.973 --> 00:03:12.762
to runt the streets of Calico as

00:03:12.762 --> 00:03:14.845
half human, half animal hybrids.

00:03:14.845 --> 00:03:17.132
- She cursed the town of Ghost Town.

00:03:17.132 --> 00:03:20.344
And every year at
Halloween time we return.

00:03:20.344 --> 00:03:22.374
- We have monsters that
return year after year.

00:03:22.374 --> 00:03:24.714
Some have been here for 20 plus years,

00:03:24.714 --> 00:03:25.999
and those seem to be the ones that

00:03:25.999 --> 00:03:27.377
develop their character the most.

00:03:27.377 --> 00:03:29.620
They build their own costumes,
and those become the icons.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.020
- We're gonna become monsters.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.409
Do you have any advice for us

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:33.859
in the transformation?
(evil laugh)

00:03:33.859 --> 00:03:35.532
- It comes from in here.

00:03:35.532 --> 00:03:37.847
It's more than just putting on a costume.

00:03:37.847 --> 00:03:39.669
(growl)

00:03:39.669 --> 00:03:41.806
Yes, I've been waiting for him!

00:03:41.806 --> 00:03:44.060
- We're gonna pick out some
nice prosthetic appliances

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:47.310
and then we're gonna do all the makeup.

00:03:50.459 --> 00:03:53.042
(upbeat music)

00:04:20.486 --> 00:04:21.986
- Three, two, one.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.551
(screams)

00:04:24.551 --> 00:04:27.782
(evil laugh)

00:04:27.782 --> 00:04:28.865
- Oh, my God!

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:32.547
I'm amazing, I'm horrifying.

00:04:32.547 --> 00:04:34.652
I'm a monster, it's
what I've always wanted.

00:04:34.652 --> 00:04:35.719
- Oh, God!

00:04:35.719 --> 00:04:36.910
Look at that!

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:38.175
Oh, look at all those teeth.

00:04:38.175 --> 00:04:40.285
I think I'm just gonna be
really excited to meet people,

00:04:40.285 --> 00:04:42.363
but I think I might
accidentally scare them away.

00:04:42.363 --> 00:04:44.331
I'm really out there to
make friends tonight.

00:04:44.331 --> 00:04:46.983
- I look kind of like a
K-Pop star got murdered.

00:04:46.983 --> 00:04:50.400
Oh, yeah, I'd (beep) me.

00:04:51.593 --> 00:04:52.897
Yeah, you're definitely the scariest.

00:04:52.897 --> 00:04:55.514
I'm the only truly scary one here.

00:04:55.514 --> 00:04:56.607
(screams)

00:04:56.607 --> 00:04:57.607
- I love it!

00:04:59.255 --> 00:05:00.818
Never change.

00:05:00.818 --> 00:05:02.323
You're beautiful, you're scary.

00:05:02.323 --> 00:05:04.847
I'm ready for school.

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:08.692
- All the blood almost makes
me look like I got a dye job.

00:05:08.692 --> 00:05:11.301
But a D-I-E job, get it?

00:05:11.301 --> 00:05:12.134
- Yeah, we got it.

00:05:12.134 --> 00:05:13.217
- It's a pun.

00:05:14.733 --> 00:05:16.545
- Guys, meet the pros.

00:05:16.545 --> 00:05:18.619
You're gonna give us your
best monster noise, okay?

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:20.702
(growls)

00:05:21.927 --> 00:05:23.184
We can do kind a catwalk thing,

00:05:23.184 --> 00:05:25.205
we're gonna see your
best monster movements.

00:05:25.205 --> 00:05:27.205
All right, there you go.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.576
What scares somebody?

00:05:29.576 --> 00:05:31.142
It's a combination of sound and movement,

00:05:31.142 --> 00:05:33.089
so let's get those quick startles.

00:05:33.089 --> 00:05:34.081
(growls)

00:05:34.081 --> 00:05:35.621
(scream)

00:05:35.621 --> 00:05:36.454
(laughs)

00:05:36.454 --> 00:05:38.562
(yells)

00:05:38.562 --> 00:05:39.860
- What about the sliders?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.832
- The sliders, then we have
these guys that go out,

00:05:41.832 --> 00:05:43.132
they glue all this metal to them,

00:05:43.132 --> 00:05:46.169
they put on knee pads, and
they just run and slide.

00:05:46.169 --> 00:05:48.597
And it's a very, very
cool, effective thing.

00:05:48.597 --> 00:05:50.819
That's a big thing that started
here at Knott's Scary Farm.

00:05:50.819 --> 00:05:53.216
The three main rules, guys,
rules of scare, ready?

00:05:53.216 --> 00:05:57.008
No touching, no dirty
talk, no foul language.

00:05:57.008 --> 00:05:59.239
- Stupid punk ass kids.

00:05:59.239 --> 00:06:01.624
- And don't break character, okay?

00:06:01.624 --> 00:06:02.457
- My wife.

00:06:03.679 --> 00:06:04.914
- Ready to tear some guests up?

00:06:04.914 --> 00:06:06.009
(cheering)

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:07.318
Let's go.

00:06:07.318 --> 00:06:09.818
(eerie music)

00:06:13.261 --> 00:06:15.511
(cackling)

00:06:28.193 --> 00:06:29.026
(yells)

00:06:29.026 --> 00:06:30.222
(laughing)

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:31.904
- So, what the (beep) was that?

00:06:31.904 --> 00:06:33.111
- Man, this is a lot tougher.

00:06:33.111 --> 00:06:34.650
People are really hard to scare.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.678
Half the people act
like they're not afraid,

00:06:36.678 --> 00:06:38.437
a quarter of the people try to heckle you.

00:06:38.437 --> 00:06:40.182
- Want to play hide-and-seek with us?

00:06:40.182 --> 00:06:41.154
- Are you triplets?

00:06:41.154 --> 00:06:43.372
- Oh, it's so ugly.

00:06:43.372 --> 00:06:45.481
- It's really hard to
actually get a scream.

00:06:45.481 --> 00:06:46.314
(yells)

00:06:46.314 --> 00:06:47.187
(giggles)

00:06:47.187 --> 00:06:48.160
Come on.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.686
- Stupid punk ass kids.

00:06:49.686 --> 00:06:51.297
- I am sweating through everything.

00:06:51.297 --> 00:06:52.261
I'm exhausted.

00:06:52.261 --> 00:06:54.059
- Turns out it takes a lot of work.

00:06:54.059 --> 00:06:55.118
It's really hard work.

00:06:55.118 --> 00:06:56.292
(yells)

00:06:56.292 --> 00:06:58.475
My throat already hurts.

00:06:58.475 --> 00:07:00.766
Keith just had (beep) story
time with all the kids.

00:07:00.766 --> 00:07:02.425
- I had a little pow-wow with some kids,

00:07:02.425 --> 00:07:03.653
had a little story time.

00:07:03.653 --> 00:07:04.587
Honestly, that was a failure

00:07:04.587 --> 00:07:06.113
because I didn't know
what to with all of them.

00:07:06.113 --> 00:07:08.041
I got them on the ground,
I'm like, "Well, now what?"

00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:09.735
I don't know.

00:07:09.735 --> 00:07:10.568
No!

00:07:10.568 --> 00:07:12.137
No, God!

00:07:12.137 --> 00:07:14.081
I know that Ned got scared a few times.

00:07:14.081 --> 00:07:15.312
(screams)

00:07:15.312 --> 00:07:16.333
- Okay.
(Laughs)

00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:18.113
okay, now we're having fun.

00:07:18.113 --> 00:07:22.034
But oh, man when you
get a total scaredy cat

00:07:22.034 --> 00:07:23.661
who's just running away--

00:07:23.661 --> 00:07:24.516
(yells)

00:07:24.516 --> 00:07:26.849
(screaming)

00:07:29.178 --> 00:07:30.490
- Do you hear those screams?

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:31.770
Those are screams of joy.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:33.976
Those are scream saying
thank you, Try Guys,

00:07:33.976 --> 00:07:35.389
for scaring the (beep) out of us.

00:07:35.389 --> 00:07:37.519
(yelling)

00:07:37.519 --> 00:07:40.624
- What was so great was
working with the other Try Guys

00:07:40.624 --> 00:07:43.350
and discovering our demon,
horror personalities.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:45.723
♫ One little penny

00:07:45.723 --> 00:07:48.318
- My demon child, he's
silent, he's creepy,

00:07:48.318 --> 00:07:50.373
and he follows you like a rain cloud.

00:07:50.373 --> 00:07:51.206
(yells)

00:07:51.206 --> 00:07:53.496
- I really liked being a
decoy because I could go and

00:07:53.496 --> 00:07:55.404
get someone's attention
and then someone can (beep)

00:07:55.404 --> 00:07:56.714
scare them from behind.

00:07:56.714 --> 00:07:58.313
(yells)

00:07:58.313 --> 00:07:59.782
- I got a few really good slides in

00:07:59.782 --> 00:08:01.212
and some really nice scares, too.

00:08:01.212 --> 00:08:02.998
(screams)

00:08:02.998 --> 00:08:05.243
- I don't know if I was
actually the scariest,

00:08:05.243 --> 00:08:07.773
but I think a lot of people
are gonna remember me.

00:08:07.773 --> 00:08:08.940
Oh, so little!

00:08:09.841 --> 00:08:10.947
- (Beep) you!

00:08:10.947 --> 00:08:12.656
(whining)

00:08:12.656 --> 00:08:14.414
- We learned an important
lesson here today:

00:08:14.414 --> 00:08:16.369
don't challenge Ned to be creepy.

00:08:16.369 --> 00:08:17.595
- My bride!

00:08:17.595 --> 00:08:19.680
I lure them in and then

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.513
(yells)

00:08:20.513 --> 00:08:22.213
(screaming)

00:08:22.213 --> 00:08:23.296
Stay with me!

00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:26.210
It's just fun.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:29.210
(suspenseful music)

00:08:35.524 --> 00:08:37.941
(chattering)

00:08:41.987 --> 00:08:42.820
Come back.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.135
I kind of felt a little bad for that girl.

00:08:49.135 --> 00:08:51.165
She was almost crying.

00:08:51.165 --> 00:08:53.166
I made a girl cry, I feel so bad.

00:08:53.166 --> 00:08:55.468
- Well, this was an
absolute dream come true.

00:08:55.468 --> 00:08:56.883
Or was it a nightmare?

00:08:56.883 --> 00:08:58.078
Same exact thing.

00:08:58.078 --> 00:08:59.688
Happy Halloween mother (beep) -ers.

00:08:59.688 --> 00:09:00.804
- This was so fun.

00:09:00.804 --> 00:09:03.004
I don't know what I was scared of.

00:09:03.004 --> 00:09:04.841
- Everybody here is just having fun.

00:09:04.841 --> 00:09:06.067
What a job this is.

00:09:06.067 --> 00:09:07.299
- It's wonderful.

00:09:07.299 --> 00:09:09.064
- You don't think about it,
but it's such a team effort.

00:09:09.064 --> 00:09:11.527
All of these amazing makeup
artists, costume designers,

00:09:11.527 --> 00:09:13.510
set designers, it's theater.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:14.909
This is straight up theater.

00:09:14.909 --> 00:09:16.760
- To be out here with the
people, to see how much work

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.041
goes into it, it was a total honor,

00:09:18.041 --> 00:09:19.505
and I'm glad that we could be apart of it.

00:09:19.505 --> 00:09:21.137
- Thank you so much to Knott's Scary Farm

00:09:21.137 --> 00:09:22.980
and all the wonderful
people who work for it.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.350
Until next time!

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:26.433
(growls)

00:09:27.671 --> 00:09:29.848
- [In Unison] Happy Halloween.

00:09:29.848 --> 00:09:32.098
(growling)

00:09:40.513 --> 00:09:42.608
- I take my coffee like I take my souls.

